          "notes": "ACADEMIC CORE\nPrepare a four-person comparison.\n\nMICRO-TOPIC MAP\nWundt • Freud • James • Dilthey\n\nSOURCE BASIS\nThe topic is retained within the uploaded NET syllabus/material framework. Use the listed source books/notes below for the detailed treatment; the website should not substitute generic explanations where the source is silent.\n\nEXAM USE\nLearn the definitions, named theorists/models, classifications, mechanisms, distinctions and source-specific examples actually present in the material.",
          "status": "Not started",
          "pyqs": "PYQ-STYLE PRACTICE 1\nQ. The year conventionally associated with Wundt's Leipzig laboratory is:\nA. 1905\nB. 1913\nC. 1879\nD. 1890\nAnswer: 1879\nNote: Generated from the source framework; this is PYQ-style practice, not a verified past-year question.\n\nPYQ-STYLE PRACTICE 2\nQ. Which approach is most directly associated with Freud?\nA. Behaviorism\nB. Psychoanalysis\nC. Functionalism\nD. Gestalt\nAnswer: Psychoanalysis\nNote: Generated from the source framework; this is PYQ-style practice, not a verified past-year question.",
          "mcqs": "Q1. The year conventionally associated with Wundt's Leipzig laboratory is:\nA. 1890\nB. 1905\nC. 1913\nD. 1879\nAnswer: 1879\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.\n\nQ2. Which approach is most directly associated with Freud?\nA. Gestalt\nB. Behaviorism\nC. Psychoanalysis\nD. Functionalism\nAnswer: Psychoanalysis\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.\n\nQ3. Which option is most directly associated with “James”?\nA. James\nB. Wundt\nC. Freud\nD. Dilthey\nAnswer: James\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.",
          "flashcards": "Q: What is Wundt?\nA: institutional emergence of experimental psychology, conventionally linked with the 1879 Leipzig laboratory\nQ: Key points for Wundt\nA: experimental psychology; Leipzig; 1879\nQ: What is Freud?\nA: psychoanalysis and psychodynamic explanations centered on unconscious processes\nQ: Key points for Freud\nA: id, ego, superego; defense mechanisms; psychosexual development\nQ: What is James?\nA: functionalism and the adaptive functions of consciousness\nQ: Key points for James\nA: William James; functionalism; stream of consciousness\nQ: What is Dilthey?\nA: understanding lived human experience through the human sciences\nQ: Key points for Dilthey\nA: Verstehen; meaning; human sciences",
