          "id": 3,
          "title": "Research Ethics",
          "explanation": "Study ethical conduct during participation, data collection, analysis, authorship and reporting. Focus on integrity, participant protection and responsible reporting.",
          "notes": "ACADEMIC CORE\nStudy ethical conduct during participation, data collection, analysis, authorship and reporting. Focus on integrity, participant protection and responsible reporting.\n\nMICRO-TOPIC MAP\nEthics in conducting research • Ethics in reporting research\n\nSOURCE BASIS\nThe topic is retained within the uploaded NET syllabus/material framework. Use the listed source books/notes below for the detailed treatment; the website should not substitute generic explanations where the source is silent.\n\nEXAM USE\nLearn the definitions, named theorists/models, classifications, mechanisms, distinctions and source-specific examples actually present in the material.",
