          "notes": "ACADEMIC CORE\nMap assessment applications to setting, purpose and decisions supported by test information.\n\nMICRO-TOPIC MAP\nClinical settings • Organizational and business settings • Educational settings • Counseling settings • Military settings\n\nSOURCE BASIS\nThe topic is retained within the uploaded NET syllabus/material framework. Use the listed source books/notes below for the detailed treatment; the website should not substitute generic explanations where the source is silent.\n\nEXAM USE\nLearn the definitions, named theorists/models, classifications, mechanisms, distinctions and source-specific examples actually present in the material.",
          "status": "Not started",
          "pyqs": "PYQ-STYLE PRACTICE 1\nQ. Which option is most directly associated with “Clinical settings”?\nA. Organizational and business settings\nB. Educational settings\nC. Counseling settings\nD. Clinical settings\nAnswer: Clinical settings\nNote: Generated from the source framework; this is PYQ-style practice, not a verified past-year question.\n\nPYQ-STYLE PRACTICE 2\nQ. Which option is most directly associated with “Organizational and business settings”?\nA. Counseling settings\nB. Organizational and business settings\nC. Clinical settings\nD. Educational settings\nAnswer: Organizational and business settings\nNote: Generated from the source framework; this is PYQ-style practice, not a verified past-year question.",
          "mcqs": "Q1. Which option is most directly associated with “Clinical settings”?\nA. Clinical settings\nB. Organizational and business settings\nC. Educational settings\nD. Counseling settings\nAnswer: Clinical settings\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.\n\nQ2. Which option is most directly associated with “Organizational and business settings”?\nA. Educational settings\nB. Counseling settings\nC. Organizational and business settings\nD. Clinical settings\nAnswer: Organizational and business settings\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.\n\nQ3. Which option is most directly associated with “Educational settings”?\nA. Organizational and business settings\nB. Counseling settings\nC. Educational settings\nD. Clinical settings\nAnswer: Educational settings\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.",
          "flashcards": "Q: What is Clinical settings?\nA: Clinical settings is a focused concept within “Applications of psychological testing in various settings: Clinical, Organizational and business, Education, Counseling, Military”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Clinical settings\nA: definition and scope of Clinical settings; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application\nQ: What is Organizational and business settings?\nA: Organizational and business settings is a focused concept within “Applications of psychological testing in various settings: Clinical, Organizational and business, Education, Counseling, Military”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Organizational and business settings\nA: definition and scope of Organizational and business settings; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application\nQ: What is Educational settings?\nA: Educational settings is a focused concept within “Applications of psychological testing in various settings: Clinical, Organizational and business, Education, Counseling, Military”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Educational settings\nA: definition and scope of Educational settings; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application\nQ: What is Counseling settings?\nA: Counseling settings is a focused concept within “Applications of psychological testing in various settings: Clinical, Organizational and business, Education, Counseling, Military”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Counseling settings\nA: definition and scope of Counseling settings; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application",
          "references": "",
          "detailed_notes": "Map assessment applications to setting, purpose and decisions supported by test information.\n\nATTACHED BOOK CONNECTION\nResearch Methods in Psychology: The book presents the scientific method as a systematic way of asking questions, forming hypotheses, collecting evidence and evaluating conclusions. It covers naturalistic observation, clinical and case-study methods, surveys, psychological testing, correlational research and experiments, including the roles of samples, populations, independent and dependent variables, control groups, random processes, reliability and validity. Correlation is treated as a relationship between variables rather than proof of causation.\nTherapy: The therapy chapter distinguishes psychologically based and biologically based approaches to helping people with mental and emotional problems. It covers psychoanalysis and free association, client-centered therapy and unconditional positive regard, behavior therapy and operant conditioning, rational-emotive behavior therapy, cognitive-behavior therapy, group approaches and major classes of psychiatric medication. Different therapies are presented as being based on different explanations of psychological difficulty.",
          "source_scope": "Authoritative UGC NET Psychology syllabus + Prompts for notes.docx + Psychology: A Self-Teaching Guide. Generated practice is PYQ-style; attached-book self-test items are source-based.",
