          "notes": "ACADEMIC CORE\nCreate an invasive versus non-invasive comparison. For each named method learn what is measured/manipulated and what kind of inference it permits.\n\nMICRO-TOPIC MAP\nAnatomical methods • Degeneration techniques • Lesion techniques • Chemical methods • Microelectrode studies • EEG • Scanning methods\n\nSOURCE BASIS\nThe topic is retained within the uploaded NET syllabus/material framework. Use the listed source books/notes below for the detailed treatment; the website should not substitute generic explanations where the source is silent.\n\nEXAM USE\nLearn the definitions, named theorists/models, classifications, mechanisms, distinctions and source-specific examples actually present in the material.",
          "status": "Not started",
          "pyqs": "PYQ-STYLE PRACTICE 1\nQ. Which option is most directly associated with “Anatomical methods”?\nA. Lesion techniques\nB. Chemical methods\nC. Anatomical methods\nD. Degeneration techniques\nAnswer: Anatomical methods\nNote: Generated from the source framework; this is PYQ-style practice, not a verified past-year question.\n\nPYQ-STYLE PRACTICE 2\nQ. Which option is most directly associated with “Degeneration techniques”?\nA. Chemical methods\nB. Degeneration techniques\nC. Anatomical methods\nD. Lesion techniques\nAnswer: Degeneration techniques\nNote: Generated from the source framework; this is PYQ-style practice, not a verified past-year question.",
