              "content_notes": "At the centre of Anatomical methods is a simple idea: Anatomical methods study the structure and organization of the nervous system. The uploaded NET material lists anatomical methods among invasive physiological-psychology methods, alongside degeneration, lesion, chemical and microelectrode techniques.\n\nThe important features are:\n• The focus is neural structure and organization.\n• They are concerned with locating or describing anatomical structures.\n• The source classifies them under physiological-psychology research methods.\n• They differ from functional methods that focus on activity or responses.\n• SOURCE BASIS\n• PowerWithin Psychology — Unit 4 Methods of Physiological Psychology.\n• COMMON EXAM TRAP\n• Anatomical methods are about structure; they should not be treated as interchangeable with methods that record moment-to-moment neural activity.\n• MEMORY CUE\n• Anatomical methods → The focus is neural structure and organization • They are concerned with locating or describing anatomical structures • The source classifies them under physiological-psychology research methods\n\nFor a NET-style question, identify the defining feature first and then distinguish it from the closest alternatives.",
