          "notes": "ACADEMIC CORE\nStudy genetic and environmental contributions to behaviour and understand why twin and adoption studies are used in the nature-nurture question.\n\nMICRO-TOPIC MAP\nChromosomal anomalies • Nature-Nurture controversy • Twin studies • Adoption studies\n\nSOURCE BASIS\nThe topic is retained within the uploaded NET syllabus/material framework. Use the listed source books/notes below for the detailed treatment; the website should not substitute generic explanations where the source is silent.\n\nEXAM USE\nLearn the definitions, named theorists/models, classifications, mechanisms, distinctions and source-specific examples actually present in the material.",
          "status": "Not started",
          "pyqs": "PYQ-STYLE PRACTICE 1\nQ. Which option is most directly associated with “Chromosomal anomalies”?\nA. Twin studies\nB. Adoption studies\nC. Chromosomal anomalies\nD. Nature-Nurture controversy\nAnswer: Chromosomal anomalies\nNote: Generated from the source framework; this is PYQ-style practice, not a verified past-year question.\n\nPYQ-STYLE PRACTICE 2\nQ. Which option is most directly associated with “Nature-Nurture controversy”?\nA. Nature-Nurture controversy\nB. Chromosomal anomalies\nC. Twin studies\nD. Adoption studies\nAnswer: Nature-Nurture controversy\nNote: Generated from the source framework; this is PYQ-style practice, not a verified past-year question.",
          "mcqs": "Q1. Which option is most directly associated with “Chromosomal anomalies”?\nA. Nature-Nurture controversy\nB. Twin studies\nC. Adoption studies\nD. Chromosomal anomalies\nAnswer: Chromosomal anomalies\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.\n\nQ2. Which option is most directly associated with “Nature-Nurture controversy”?\nA. Adoption studies\nB. Nature-Nurture controversy\nC. Chromosomal anomalies\nD. Twin studies\nAnswer: Nature-Nurture controversy\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.\n\nQ3. Which option is most directly associated with “Twin studies”?\nA. Adoption studies\nB. Twin studies\nC. Chromosomal anomalies\nD. Nature-Nurture controversy\nAnswer: Twin studies\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.",
          "flashcards": "Q: What is Chromosomal anomalies?\nA: Chromosomal anomalies is a focused concept within “Genetics and behavior: Chromosomal anomalies; Nature-Nurture controversy (Twin studies and adoption studies)”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Chromosomal anomalies\nA: definition and scope of Chromosomal anomalies; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application\nQ: What is Nature-Nurture controversy?\nA: Nature-Nurture controversy is a focused concept within “Genetics and behavior: Chromosomal anomalies; Nature-Nurture controversy (Twin studies and adoption studies)”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Nature-Nurture controversy\nA: definition and scope of Nature-Nurture controversy; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application\nQ: What is Twin studies?\nA: comparison of monozygotic and dizygotic twins to estimate genetic and environmental contributions\nQ: Key points for Twin studies\nA: MZ vs DZ; heritability; environmental assumptions\nQ: What is Adoption studies?\nA: Adoption studies is a focused concept within “Genetics and behavior: Chromosomal anomalies; Nature-Nurture controversy (Twin studies and adoption studies)”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Adoption studies\nA: definition and scope of Adoption studies; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application",
          "references": "",
          "detailed_notes": "Study genetic and environmental contributions to behaviour and understand why twin and adoption studies are used in the nature-nurture question.\n\nATTACHED BOOK CONNECTION\nBiology of Behavior: The biology chapter explains how the nervous and endocrine systems contribute to behavior. It covers neuron structure and communication, neural impulses, synaptic transmission and neurotransmitters, and distinguishes central and peripheral nervous-system functions. It also introduces major brain structures, the autonomic nervous system, endocrine glands and biological influences on behavior such as arousal, stress, sleep and reproduction.",
