          "flashcards": "Q: What is Gestalt approach?\nA: Gestalt approach is a focused concept within “Approaches to the Study of Perception: Gestalt and physiological approaches”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Gestalt approach\nA: definition and scope of Gestalt approach; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application\nQ: What is Physiological approach?\nA: Physiological approach is a focused concept within “Approaches to the Study of Perception: Gestalt and physiological approaches”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Physiological approach\nA: definition and scope of Physiological approach; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application",
          "references": "",
          "detailed_notes": "Compare Gestalt explanations with physiological approaches to perception.\n\nATTACHED BOOK CONNECTION\nPerception: The perception chapter examines how sensory information becomes an organized psychological experience. It covers the distinction between the geographical and psychological worlds, Gestalt organization and figure-ground perception, perceptual learning, constancies and illusions, and binocular and monocular depth cues. It also discusses movement perception and the status of unusual perceptual claims such as psi powers within scientific psychology.",
