              "title": "Interference theory",
              "content_notes": "At the centre of Interference theory is a simple idea: forgetting through competition between memories.\n\nThe important features are:\n• Proactive: old → new\n• Retroactive: new → old\n\nThe exam distinction is important: PRO = prior blocks new; RETRO = recent blocks old.\n\nWhen this micro-topic appears in a NET-style question, read the alternatives against the defining idea first. The source framework emphasises The source framework emphasizes identification, comparison, application and statement-based questions. Practise one short scenario and one confusion pair.",
