              "content_notes": "At the centre of Motivated forgetting is a simple idea: Motivated forgetting treats forgetting in relation to psychological motives and avoidance of distressing material, alongside nonmotivational mechanisms such as encoding failure, decay and interference.\n\nThe important features are:\n• Core definition and mechanism\n• Closest distinction or comparison\n• Relevant learning/memory framework\n• DISTINCTION / CAUTION\n• Do not assume every forgotten memory is deliberately repressed.\n• SOURCE BASIS\n• Baron & Misra\n• Psychology: A Self-Teaching Guide\n• STUDY RULE\n• Use the source terminology and identify the mechanism before selecting an answer.\n\nFor a NET-style question, identify the defining feature first and then distinguish it from the closest alternatives.",
