              "title": "Rotter's Locus of Control",
              "content_notes": "At the centre of Rotter's Locus of Control is a simple idea: expectancy that outcomes are controlled internally or externally.\n\nThe important features are:\n• Internal locus\n• External locus\n• Expectancy\n\nThe exam distinction is important: Internal locus does not mean total control.\n\nWhen this micro-topic appears in a NET-style question, read the alternatives against the defining idea first. The source framework emphasises The source framework emphasizes identification, comparison, application and statement-based questions. Practise one short scenario and one confusion pair.",
