              "deep_learning": "At the centre of Affiliation is a simple idea: Affiliation motivation concerns the desire for social connection, acceptance and positive relationships. The uploaded sources place affiliation among acquired motives and McClelland's needs.\n\nThese features should be learned as parts of one psychological idea rather than as disconnected facts. Affiliation involves desire for interpersonal connection. Acceptance and belonging can motivate behavior. Affiliation can influence choices and persistence in social settings. It differs from achievement and power motives. SOURCE BASIS. Ciccarelli & White — McClelland's Needs; Self-Teaching Guide — Acquired Motives. COMMON EXAM TRAP. Affiliation is about relationship and belonging needs, not merely social activity frequency. MEMORY CUE. Affiliation → Affiliation involves desire for interpersonal connection • Acceptance and belonging can motivate behavior • Affiliation can influence choices and persistence in social settings.\n\nSource grounding: Ciccarelli & White — McClelland's Needs; Self-Teaching Guide — Acquired Motives.",
