          "status": "Not started",
          "pyqs": "PYQ-STYLE PRACTICE 1\nQ. Which option is most directly associated with “Motivational competence”?\nA. None of the above\nB. Motivational competence\nC. None of the above\nD. None of the above\nAnswer: Motivational competence\nNote: Generated from the source framework; this is PYQ-style practice, not a verified past-year question.",
          "mcqs": "Q1. Which option is most directly associated with “Motivational competence”?\nA. None of the above\nB. None of the above\nC. Motivational competence\nD. None of the above\nAnswer: Motivational competence\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.",
          "flashcards": "Q: What is Motivational competence?\nA: Motivational competence is a focused concept within “Motivational Competence”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Motivational competence\nA: definition and scope of Motivational competence; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application",
          "references": "",
          "detailed_notes": "Study this as the ability to mobilize and regulate motivation in relation to goals and behaviour, keeping the term within the syllabus context.\n\nATTACHED BOOK CONNECTION\nMotivation: The motivation chapter treats motives as forces behind action and explains their interaction with learning. It distinguishes biological drives from general and acquired motives, discusses unconscious motivation, and examines needs such as autonomy, achievement and related motives. The chapter also introduces Maslow's self-actualization and Frankl's emphasis on meaning, linking motivation with broader questions about purpose and human potential.",
          "source_scope": "Authoritative UGC NET Psychology syllabus + Prompts for notes.docx + Psychology: A Self-Teaching Guide. Generated practice is PYQ-style; attached-book self-test items are source-based.",
