          "references": "",
          "detailed_notes": "Study psychological conflict, its sources and major types as specified in the syllabus.\n\nATTACHED BOOK CONNECTION\nEmotions: The emotions chapter treats emotions as experiences that include motivational, physiological and psychological dimensions. It examines basic dimensions of emotion, major theories including James-Lange and competing approaches, and the relationship between emotion, action and cognition. It also covers stress and health, including chronic stress and Type A behavior, and explains approach-approach, approach-avoidance, double approach-avoidance and avoidance-avoidance conflicts.",
