          "explanation": "Build a clear understanding of Stress Management Strategies, then connect its key ideas, distinctions, and applications.",
          "notes": "ACADEMIC CORE\nBuild a clear understanding of Stress Management Strategies, then connect its key ideas, distinctions, and applications.\n\nMICRO-TOPIC MAP\nBiofeedback • Music therapy • Breathing exercises • Progressive Muscular Relaxation • Guided Imagery • Mindfulness • Meditation • Yogasana • Stress Inoculation Training\n\nSOURCE BASIS\nThe topic is retained within the uploaded NET syllabus/material framework. Use the listed source books/notes below for the detailed treatment; the website should not substitute generic explanations where the source is silent.\n\nEXAM USE\nLearn the definitions, named theorists/models, classifications, mechanisms, distinctions and source-specific examples actually present in the material.",
          "status": "Not started",
          "pyqs": "PYQ-STYLE PRACTICE 1\nQ. Which option is most directly associated with “Biofeedback”?\nA. Biofeedback\nB. Music therapy\nC. Breathing exercises\nD. Progressive Muscular Relaxation\nAnswer: Biofeedback\nNote: Generated from the source framework; this is PYQ-style practice, not a verified past-year question.\n\nPYQ-STYLE PRACTICE 2\nQ. Which option is most directly associated with “Music therapy”?\nA. Progressive Muscular Relaxation\nB. Music therapy\nC. Biofeedback\nD. Breathing exercises\nAnswer: Music therapy\nNote: Generated from the source framework; this is PYQ-style practice, not a verified past-year question.",
          "mcqs": "Q1. Which option is most directly associated with “Biofeedback”?\nA. Progressive Muscular Relaxation\nB. Biofeedback\nC. Music therapy\nD. Breathing exercises\nAnswer: Biofeedback\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.\n\nQ2. Which option is most directly associated with “Music therapy”?\nA. Breathing exercises\nB. Progressive Muscular Relaxation\nC. Music therapy\nD. Biofeedback\nAnswer: Music therapy\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.\n\nQ3. Which option is most directly associated with “Breathing exercises”?\nA. Progressive Muscular Relaxation\nB. Breathing exercises\nC. Biofeedback\nD. Music therapy\nAnswer: Breathing exercises\nExplanation: Review the micro-topic note for the defining feature, key distinction and application.",
          "flashcards": "Q: What is Biofeedback?\nA: Biofeedback is a focused concept within “Stress management strategies: Biofeedback, Music therapy, Breathing exercises, Progressive Muscular Relaxation, Guided Imagery, Mindfulness, Meditation, Yogasana, Stress Inoculation Training”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Biofeedback\nA: definition and scope of Biofeedback; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application\nQ: What is Music therapy?\nA: Music therapy is a focused concept within “Stress management strategies: Biofeedback, Music therapy, Breathing exercises, Progressive Muscular Relaxation, Guided Imagery, Mindfulness, Meditation, Yogasana, Stress Inoculation Training”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Music therapy\nA: definition and scope of Music therapy; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application\nQ: What is Breathing exercises?\nA: Breathing exercises is a focused concept within “Stress management strategies: Biofeedback, Music therapy, Breathing exercises, Progressive Muscular Relaxation, Guided Imagery, Mindfulness, Meditation, Yogasana, Stress Inoculation Training”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Breathing exercises\nA: definition and scope of Breathing exercises; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application\nQ: What is Progressive Muscular Relaxation?\nA: Progressive Muscular Relaxation is a focused concept within “Stress management strategies: Biofeedback, Music therapy, Breathing exercises, Progressive Muscular Relaxation, Guided Imagery, Mindfulness, Meditation, Yogasana, Stress Inoculation Training”. Prepare it as an exam-sized learning node: define it, identify its key features, distinguish it from a close concept, and apply it to one short example.\nQ: Key points for Progressive Muscular Relaxation\nA: definition and scope of Progressive Muscular Relaxation; key features/components/stages as applicable; one comparison or common confusion; one example or application",
          "references": "",
          "detailed_notes": "\n\nATTACHED BOOK CONNECTION\nEmotions: The emotions chapter treats emotions as experiences that include motivational, physiological and psychological dimensions. It examines basic dimensions of emotion, major theories including James-Lange and competing approaches, and the relationship between emotion, action and cognition. It also covers stress and health, including chronic stress and Type A behavior, and explains approach-approach, approach-avoidance, double approach-avoidance and avoidance-avoidance conflicts.",
          "source_scope": "Authoritative UGC NET Psychology syllabus + Prompts for notes.docx + Psychology: A Self-Teaching Guide. Generated practice is PYQ-style; attached-book self-test items are source-based.",
