              "title": "Group dynamics",
              "content_notes": "At the centre of Group dynamics is a simple idea: Group dynamics concerns the patterns of interaction, roles, norms, cohesion and influence that develop within groups. The uploaded NET material places group dynamics alongside leadership and social influence.\n\nThe important features are:\n• Groups develop norms and roles.\n• Cohesion can affect interaction and performance.\n• Members influence one another.\n• Group processes can facilitate or hinder decision making.\n• SOURCE BASIS\n• PowerWithin Psychology — Group Dynamics and Leadership; Kaplan AP Psychology — Groups.\n• COMMON EXAM TRAP\n• Group dynamics is broader than group size; it concerns interaction patterns and processes within the group.\n• MEMORY CUE\n• Group dynamics → Groups develop norms and roles • Cohesion can affect interaction and performance • Members influence one another\n\nFor a NET-style question, identify the defining feature first and then distinguish it from the closest alternatives.",
